<div style="text-align: center;">
<h2><span>WHEN <span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>YOU</strong></span> HAVE THE <span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>WILL,</strong></span> DON'T SAY <span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>NEVER!</strong></span> JUST <span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>LEAVE</strong></span> THOSE THOUGHTS!</span></h2>
<p>- <a href="https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/baldis-basics-in-education-and-learning/images/f/f4/WeirdMessage-sharedassets2.assets-273.png/revision/latest?cb=20190406101547">Baldi's Basics Birthday Bash</a></p>
</div>
<hr />
<p><span style="color: purple"><strong>Thanks for reading, pal!</strong></span></p>
<p>Started writing this 3 Apr 2020.</p>
<p>I came up with this idea half-asleep. It's heavily inspired by the SCPs that I read in my dreams, which usually end up being really format-screwy cause of dream logic. Think of this as if you were dreaming of a bizarre cartoonish version of The SCP Foundation universe, and this was the obligatory virtual reality episode.</p>
<p>Sometimes, when I fall asleep, I have dreams where I am reading the SCP Wiki. They're usually really odd dreams, and when I'm reading, the SCPs are usually really weird and don't seem to have much of a motive. I remember one dream I was having where I was reading an article about evil muppets that attacked people just cause they wanted to. The image was a blurry muppet running at the cameraman. There's a certain feeling that's hard to capture when I'm in a dream. I hope I captured it here. This is how people seem to talk in my dreams, this is how entities seem to act in my dreams. Idk, I'm rambling.</p>
<p>This isn't meant to be taken too seriously. The idea is uhh, really fucking silly and dumb, at least, that's how I see it. But it also means a lot to me. Sorry if you don't enjoy it, I get that feeling.</p>
<p>HUGE thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/westrin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2858989); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2858989&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1590647425" alt="Westrin" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2858989)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/westrin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2858989); return false;">Westrin</a></span> and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/validclay" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4538622); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4538622&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1590647425" alt="ValidClay" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4538622)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/validclay" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4538622); return false;">ValidClay</a></span> for being my collab partners on this. Without you amazing people, I wouldn't have been able to get this idea off the ground! I'm immensely grateful.</p>
<p>For anyone wondering, no, this SCP is not a reference to Goat Simulator. I hate that game.</p>
<p>If you do a reading of this, you have to say I'm sexy and cool at the beginning. Say that about my collab partners too! That's the rules.</p>
<p><strong>And a message to NewScapePro, do not use this SCP in your Minecraft Roleplays.</strong></p>
<p>Update: I want to thank <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sekai-s" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4476849); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4476849&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1590647425" alt="Sekai_s" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4476849)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sekai-s" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4476849); return false;">Sekai_s</a></span> for letting me use their title CSS for my SCP title! (The SCP in question that uses this title CSS is <a href="http://scp-int.wikidot.com/scp-cn-1109/">SCP-CN-1109.</a> (I removed it after a while for reasons that are hard to describe but it wasn't because of any conflict, and I'm still really happy that they gave me permission to use it!)</p>
