<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;My&nbsp;Thoughts&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Rating</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;My&nbsp;Thoughts&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Rating</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I liked this a lot. I'm glad to see this hit the mainlist after hearing cryptic whispers about it for the past month or so.</p>
<p>Parts of the documentation came off as clunky, and there were some issues I had with the dialogue (see Critique section below), but they were not enough to detract from the article as a whole.</p>
<p>I <em>especially</em> liked the changing images. I've seen the &quot;click to enlarge&quot; image swap trick before, but leading to an entire offset was unexpected. Afterwards, I went through and enlarged every image to find if anything was different. I was not disappointed.</p>
<p>+1, pretty easily.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Suggestions&nbsp;[Warning:&nbsp;Long]</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Suggestions&nbsp;[Warning:&nbsp;Long]</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>There's one general SPaG comment that I don't have the time nor effort to manually point out each instance of: a <em>lot</em> of commas are missing throughout the dialogue sections. I understand that, to replicate naturalistic speech, some commas can be sacrificed&#8212;but there are many cases in this article where it would actually have a verbal pause where a comma has been left out.</p>
<p>Anyways, on to some specific lines:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5045 is a virtual reality game that is compatible with most virtual reality headsets titled &quot;Goat VR.&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Makes it sound like SCP-5045 is compatible with &quot;virtual reality headsets that are titled 'Goat VR'&quot;. I obviously know what you meant, but the wording is jarring. I recommend restructuring it as:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5045 is a virtual reality game titled &quot;Goat VR&quot; that is compatible with most virtual reality headsets.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Within the farmhouse is a crudely drawn humanoid entity, with slightly more visual detail <strong>then</strong> the goats,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Than.<br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>D-1711:</strong> Very well then.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Feels&#8230; wooden.<br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>D-1711:</strong> Alright… uhh, everything's all black and outlined in these bright neon colors&#8230; <em>[snip]</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>They're rattling off the exact details from the Description section. You can afford to cut most of this and leave it as &quot;bright neon colors&quot;.<br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>SCP-5045-1:</strong> Very well then.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Another &quot;very well then&quot;, but this one feels a <em>bit</em> more characteristic. Doesn't really fit the Texan drawl, I don't think, but that might be me.<br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>D-6770:</strong> My name is ████████ ██████. What's yours?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That's two names under those blackboxes. It would be <em>weird</em> to meet someone who's mid-panic attack and give them your full name.<br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>D-6770:</strong> -nd it's always nice to have company, you know? I'm glad you're here.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There's no reason to cut in mid-word, especially when we know what they said. Cutting in at &quot;-and&quot; would make more sense.<br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>D-6770:</strong> I'm not letting you lay a fucking hair on him. Wait, did I say hair? I meant han-</p>
</blockquote>
<p>As much as I do like this line, it feels weird under pressure to go &quot;wait, did I say hair?&quot; when there's present danger. Recommend changing it to something more like:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>D-6770:</strong> I'm not letting you lay a fucking hair on him. I mean, han-</p>
</blockquote>
<p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>SCP-5045-1:</strong> <em>[snip]</em> Could you please put on the headset? It'll help me out a ton…<br />
<strong>Researcher Ivan Hovnyuk:</strong> You're just trying to get me to put the headset on, aren't you?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yes, obviously, as Farmer just said so.<br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br />
That about wraps up everything that jumped out at me as no-good.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

